# Python in Excel time series functions

Time series functions operate on an ordered series (`expsmooth`, `stl`, `stl_plot`, `resid_analysis`, `arima_order`, `zscore_replace`, forecasting, seasonal decomposition, and similar). `describe`, `corr`, `normality_check`, `cluster_prep`, and sampling functions are not time series.

## Init files

Copy the same `def` and quoted call into **both**:

1. @source/python-in-excel/init/PaulPythonLibrary.py (full library)
2. @source/python-in-excel/init/TimeSeries.py (time-series-only Initialization)

Do not add time series functions to @source/python-in-excel/init/DefaultInitialization.py.

Keep the two copies identical. `TimeSeries.py` is a complete Initialization: Excel default imports, then time series `def`s only (including shared helpers such as `stl_fit`).

```python
# ❌ BAD — time series function only in PaulPythonLibrary.py
# ✅ GOOD — same def in functions/name.py, PaulPythonLibrary.py, and TimeSeries.py
```

Then follow @.cursor/rules/python-in-excel.mdc (function file, PythonMap, README, CHANGELOG, tests, docs).
